Project Specification and Development Prompt
Web-Based Surgical Robotics Simulation for Medical Education
1. Project Overview
Develop an interactive, web-based educational simulation inspired by the da Vinci 5 robotic surgical system.

The application is designed for first-year medical students who have no prior knowledge of robotics, programming, or robotic surgery.

The primary objective is to introduce students to basic concepts of robotic surgical instrument control and object manipulation through an intuitive, interactive 3D simulation.

This is an educational demonstration, not a clinically accurate surgical simulator. Do not claim to reproduce the actual mechanical design, proprietary software, kinematics, or clinical performance of the da Vinci 5 system.

The application must be simple, visually engaging, easy to understand, and optimized for iPad and tablet use.

Main concept
The application provides two synchronized visual perspectives:

Doctor View: A simulated endoscopic perspective showing the virtual surgical workspace and instrument tip.

Robot View: A 3D visualization of a simplified robotic arm showing its movement and instrument configuration.

Students control the virtual robotic instrument using large touchscreen buttons and complete guided missions.

