Architecture: Level 1 — Independent Simulation
The application must use a client-side simulation architecture.

Requirements:

No user registration or login.

No backend server for simulation.

No database.

No classroom management system.

No real-time communication between students.

Each student's simulation runs independently in their own browser.

Each student's robot state is isolated from other users.

Save individual progress using localStorage.

The application must remain functional without a database.

The server should primarily deliver the application and static assets. Robot calculations, mission progression, and 3D visualization should run in the student's browser.

Design the software architecture so that a backend and teacher dashboard could be added in the future without rebuilding the simulation engine.

