7.3 Synchronization
Doctor View and Robot View must always represent exactly the same simulation state.

For example:

When the instrument moves right, both views must show rightward movement.

When the instrument moves upward, both views must show upward movement.

When the instrument moves forward, both views must show increased depth.

When the gripper closes, both views must show the same gripper state.

When an object is grasped, both views must represent the attachment.

Implement one shared robot state as the source of truth.

Do not implement independent movement systems for the two views.

