10. Guided Instruction System
This is one of the most important features.

Every mission must contain several sequential guided steps.

Students should never have to guess what to do next.

Each guided step should contain:

Instruction text.

Relevant control highlighted.

Target or object highlighted.

Success condition.

Confirmation message.

Automatic progression to the next step.

Example
Instruction:

"Move the instrument tip to the RIGHT target."

Expected visual feedback:

RIGHT button pulses gently.

Right target in Doctor View is highlighted.

Instrument movement is visible in both views.

When the instrument reaches the target, movement is no longer required.

Success message:

"Target reached!"

After success:

Stop the button animation.

Highlight the success state.

Display a green confirmation message.

Optionally play a subtle confirmation sound.

Wait briefly.

Automatically advance to the next instruction.

Visual guidance rules
Use three types of visual cues:

Control cue

Gentle blinking or pulsing of the required button.

Approximately 0.8–1.0 second animation interval.

Target cue

Highlight the target area.

Use a gentle glow or outline.

Success cue

Green confirmation.

Short success message.

Optional subtle sound.

Never blink all controls simultaneously.

Only highlight the control required by the current instruction.

Provide:

Show Instruction Again.

Pause.

Reset Current Mission.

Respect reduced-motion settings.

11. Task 1: Basic Instrument Control
Objective:

Introduce students to directional movement and instrument positioning.

This task contains five missions.

Mission 1: Move Right
Objective:
Move the instrument tip to the right target.

Guided steps:

Identify the right target.

Press and hold RIGHT.

Move until the instrument enters the target zone.

Automatically detect success.

Success message:

"Great! You have reached the right target."

Mission 2: Move Left
Objective:
Move the instrument tip to the left target.

Guided steps:

Identify the left target.

Press and hold LEFT.

Move until the instrument enters the target zone.

Automatically detect success.

Success message:

"Great! You have reached the left target."

Mission 3: Move Up and Down
Objective:
Understand vertical movement.

Guided steps:

Identify the upper target.

Press UP until the target is reached.

Identify the lower target.

Press DOWN until the target is reached.

Success message:

"Excellent! You can control vertical movement."

Mission 4: Move Forward and Backward
Objective:
Understand depth movement.

Guided steps:

Identify the far target.

Press FORWARD until the target is reached.

Identify the near target.

Press BACKWARD until the target is reached.

Success message:

"Excellent! You can control instrument depth."

Mission 5: Combined Movement
Objective:
Introduce combined horizontal and vertical movement.

Guided steps:

Identify the final target.

Move horizontally and vertically using the directional controls.

Reach the target while avoiding obstacles.

Automatically detect success.

Success message:

"Well done! You have completed Basic Instrument Control."

12. Task 2: Object Manipulation
Objective:

Introduce the basic principles of robotic gripping and object manipulation.

Create a simple virtual workspace containing:

One colored object.

Robotic instrument with gripper.

Starting position.

Destination zone.

Clearly visible object and target.

This task contains five missions.

Mission 1: Approach Object
Objective:
Move the instrument tip toward the object.

Guided steps:

Identify the object.

Move the instrument toward the object.

Stop when the gripper reaches the grasping zone.

Success message:

"Object reached. Ready to grasp."

Mission 2: Grasp Object
Objective:
Close the robotic gripper around the object.

Guided steps:

Confirm the instrument is inside the grasping zone.

Press CLOSE GRIPPER.

Attach the object to the gripper.

Confirm successful grasping.

Success message:

"Object successfully grasped!"

The object should follow the gripper after successful grasping.

Mission 3: Lift Object
Objective:
Move the grasped object upward.

Guided steps:

Identify the required lifting height.

Press UP.

Move the object to the designated height.

Automatically detect success.

Success message:

"Object lifted successfully!"

Mission 4: Transfer Object
Objective:
Move the object to the destination zone.

Guided steps:

Identify the destination.

Move horizontally and in depth.

Keep the object attached to the gripper.

Enter the destination zone.

Success message:

"Object successfully transferred!"

Mission 5: Release Object
Objective:
Release the object inside the destination zone.

Guided steps:

Confirm the object is inside the destination zone.

Press OPEN GRIPPER.

Detach the object.

Confirm that it remains inside the destination zone.

Success message:

"Congratulations! You have completed Object Manipulation."

The object should remain at its released position.

