14. Success Detection
Implement automatic success detection.

Examples:

Right or left movement: instrument tip enters the corresponding target zone.

Up or down movement: instrument reaches the target height.

Forward or backward movement: instrument reaches the required depth.

Combined movement: instrument reaches the target without entering an obstacle zone.

Grasping: gripper closes while the tip is within the grasping zone.

Lifting: object reaches the required height while attached.

Transfer: object enters the destination zone.

Release: gripper opens and object remains inside the destination zone.

Use configurable position tolerances.

Success conditions should be evaluated using the simulation state, not visual appearance alone.

Provide a clear visual indication of success.

